    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d106">

                <pb facs="0144" n="134" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg134"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/5–2147: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-05-21T10:00:00+09:00">May 21, 1947—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 21—7 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1103. Available information indicates Communist forces Manchuria have assumed
                    initiative and mounted sizable offensive from east and west against Changchun
                    area. Although Changchun airfield under attack from Communist militia units
                    night May 17 and Communist cavalry patrols operating within 7 kilometers of
                    city, it seems unlikely at this juncture that Communists have intention or
                    capability of occupying Changchun. It seems probable that Communists will
                    endeavor harass Government line communication and supply south of Changchun with
                    intent cause further attrition Government strength which may eventually force
                    Government withdrawal southward.</p>
                <p>Well coordinated plan is indicated by large scale raid Changli area May 18
                    (reference Embassy telegram 1088, May 19<anchor n="4" xml:id="d106-f1"/>).
                    Possibility also exists that interdiction rail line Changli is forerunner to
                    attack on major Government supply base for Manchuria at Hulutao.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
